  "prompt": [
    "Client: Harbourline Commerce, a multi-tenant retail order platform with about 400 tenants. Database hlc-orders-prod: Azure SQL Database, Business Critical, Gen5, 16 vCores, compatibility level 160, READ_COMMITTED_SNAPSHOT ON. All times are UTC. Business hours are 07:30 to 18:00. The nightly batch must finish by 06:00. Evidence was collected from Mon 21 Sep to Sun 27 Sep 2026.",
    "The CTO writes: 'In the day we get random 30-second timeouts. Some days are fine and some days are awful, and CPU",
    "shows 100% in the portal.' The dashboard calls GetOrdersDashboard with TOP 50 and a 7-day range, about 6 times per",
    "second at peak. The nightly batch step 'TenantReport' calls the same method with a 365-day range and TOP 100000, about",
    "140 times for tenant 1, which holds about 18% of dbo.Orders. TenantReport ran 06:04-06:58 on Tue 22, 06:57-08:05 on",
    "Wed 23, 05:52-06:46 on Thu 24 and 05:57-06:52 on Fri 25. Parameter sensitive plan optimization is ON (compatibility",
    "level 160). Name the root cause of the bad days."
  ],
